[32m+[m[32m## API probe scripts (`test/`)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`test/*.py` are **not** unit tests — there is no test suite. They are standalone, stdlib-only[m
[32m+[m[32mscripts that make **live** Apibara calls to pin down the API's real field shapes, and write raw[m
[32m+[m[32mJSON to `test_run/` (gitignored). Each burns 1–2 of the 100/month free-plan budget, so the cost is[m
[32m+[m[32mstated in every docstring. They import nothing from `app/` and resolve `.env` / `test_run/` off[m
[32m+[m[32mtheir own file location, so they run from any working directory.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mpython test/test_apibara.py                 # 2 calls — original probe: Lexus IS 350 + Audi A4[m
[32m+[m[32mpython test/test_apibara_search01.py        # 2 calls — Lexus ES 350 + Audi S5, per_page=20[m
[32m+[m[32mpython test/test_apibara_history01.py       # 1-2 calls — prior auction runs for one VIN[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m./test/run_sold.sh iaai                     # 1 call  — sold IAAI lots + IAAI-only filters[m
[32m+[m[32m./test/run_sold.sh copart                   # 1 call  — sold Copart lots[m
[32m+[m[32m./test/run_sold.sh generic                  # 2 calls — ended lots + one /history lookup[m
[32m+[m[32m./test/run_sold.sh all                      # 4 calls — all three[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`run_sold.sh` prints the quota cost and asks for confirmation before spending anything.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mServer-side filters live in a `PARAMS` / `SEARCHES` constant at the top of each script;[m
[32m+[m[32mclient-side filters (`BODY_STYLES`, `EXCLUDE_DAMAGE`, `SELLER_TYPES`) are separate constants,[m
[32m+[m[32mbecause Apibara has **no body-style parameter** and its `damage` filter is include-only with an[m
[32m+[m[32menum that cannot express collision damage. Sold/ended lots come from `lot_sub_status=Ended`[m
[32m+[m[32m(*not* `lot_status`, which only accepts `All` / `Timed` / `Buy Now`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhat these scripts established, verified against 60 live records:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Prior sale attempts** are not in the search payload — only a single `last_sold_*` snapshot.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Full run history needs `GET /vehicles/{VIN}/history` (bare VIN or lot number, **not** the[m
[32m+[m[32m  record's `slug_vin`), 1 call per VIN, returning `{platform, date, price, status}` per run.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **`status` is a bid outcome, not a transaction.** `"Sold on Approval"` means the high bid missed[m
[32m+[m[32m  the seller's reserve. Lots marked `"Sold"` demonstrably relist afterwards.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Reserve prices are not published** by any field; they can only be bounded from history[m
[32m+[m[32m  (on-approval rows sit below the reserve).[m
[32m+[m[32m- **IAAI records are far richer than Copart's**: `ActualCashValue` (27/27), `EstimatedRepairCost`[m
[32m+[m[32m  (17/27), `body_style` (27/27) and a pre-bidder count all come from IAAI's `details` block.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Copart records have **no `details` block at all**.[m
